  "final_source_delta": {
    "note": "The closed set of src/** contracts whose compiled bytes are allowed to differ from the immutable C4 capture above. bin/freeze-artifacts.py check requires every contract named here to ACTUALLY differ, so this record can never become a standing exemption, and requires every contract not named here to equal C4 byte for byte. That is what proves the ticket sequence through regent-alv1.10 touched exactly the factory, the strategy, the splitter and the receiver, and left the escrow and the fee hook byte-identical. It proves which production bytes moved; the source diff and independent review prove why.",
    "ticket": "regent-alv1.10",
    "changed": [
      {
        "key": "src/revenue/SubjectSplitterV1.sol:SubjectSplitterV1",
        "reason": "regent-alv1.7.1 deleted the recoveryAdmin binding, its getter, its modifier, its NotRecoveryAdmin error and its initializer argument, made both recovery entry points permissionless, amount-free and whole-balance to the immutable treasury, and shortened SplitterInitialized and initialize to six fields; SPL-017, SPL-018 and ABI-005 carry that behaviour and ABI-012 carries the deleted selectors. regent-alv1.10 then divides each post-skim net by fixed total-supply coverage — stakers collectively receive floor(net * totalStaked / 100_000_000_000e18) through the existing accumulator and the immutable treasury immediately receives the exact remainder — and requires a later block than an account's own latest stake before any partial or complete unstake, adding error SameBlockUnstake() as the only new ABI member and a private per-account stake-block mapping with no getter. SPL-005, SPL-006, SPL-009, SPL-013, HOK-011, INV-002 and ABI-004 carry that behaviour."
      },
      {
        "key": "src/revenue/PaymentReceiverV1.sol:PaymentReceiverV1",
        "reason": "The same deletion on the receiver: the recoveryAdmin binding read from the splitter, its getter, its modifier and its NotRecoveryAdmin error are gone, and both recovery entry points become permissionless, amount-free and whole-balance to the immutable treasury. RCV-009, RCV-010, RCV-011 and ABI-006 carry the behaviour."
      },
      {
        "key": "src/strategy/RegentLBPStrategy.sol:RegentLBPStrategy",
        "reason": "DistributionParams and Distribution lose their recoveryAdmin field, RecoveryAdminHasNoCode(address) is deleted, the splitter initializer call loses its seventh argument, one private launch-time treasury admission refusing exactly six shared-system addresses is added between escrow authentication and auction creation, both per-launch clones stay on the pinned upstream ordinary LibClone.clone, and the pinned planner's two CONTRACT_BALANCE settlement amounts are replaced with the exact amounts this graduation funds. STR-019, FAC-028, MIG-003 and MIG-022 carry the behaviour."
      },
      {
        "key": "src/factory/RegentsAutolaunchFactoryV1.sol:RegentsAutolaunchFactoryV1",
        "reason": "LaunchParams, the Launch record and LaunchCreated lose their recoveryAdmin field, the launch-record readback renumbers accordingly, and SPLITTER_IMPLEMENTATION_RUNTIME_CODE_HASH and RECEIVER_IMPLEMENTATION_RUNTIME_CODE_HASH are updated to the corrected clone runtimes. regent-alv1.10 moves SPLITTER_IMPLEMENTATION_RUNTIME_CODE_HASH once more, to the runtime the supply-coverage splitter compiles to, so the factory's existing constructor admission keeps admitting the real implementation; no selector, field, event or other factory behaviour changes with it. ABI-002, ABI-003, ABI-007, ABI-011 and DEP-060 carry it."
      }
    ]
  },
